<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution</p><h1 class="enc-title">French Revolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1789">1789</a>–<a href="/years/1799">1799</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The French Revolution was the period of upheaval in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> that began with the meeting of the Estates-General in 1789, abolished the monarchy in 1792 and ended with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon Bonaparte</a>'s seizure of power in 1799. Its ideas of popular <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a>, equality and the rights of man spread far beyond France, inspiring settlers at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/graaff-reinet">Graaff-Reinet</a> and Swellendam, while the wars it began reshaped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and its colonies for a generation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/french-revolution.jpg" alt="French Revolution" width="320" height="252" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anonymous_-_Prise_de_la_Bastille.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
